# Read directly by cli.py (see _load_local_env()) so Hermes' sandboxed container has these
# without depending on broker/hermes.py's env-var forwarding into Docker, which turned out to
# be unreliable in practice. This file rides along with the module's existing read-only bind
# mount (modules/registry.py), so it's always present inside the container regardless of risk.
#
# Copy this to .env in this same directory and fill in the values from bot/server/.env.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
